Glyphka

A generative lettering and symbol studio by Plinka.

Run
  bun install --frozen-lockfile
  bun run dev

Development uses port 8401. The application builds independently of any
other checkout.

Check
  bun run check
  bun run test:browser

Build
  bun run build

The static site is generated in dist/.

Lettering
  A-Z, digits and . - +. Sixteen visual families. Continuous mutation,
  weight, rounding, width, slant, spacing and transparent cutouts.
  The die generates another direction. Each letter has further drawings
  through the More drawings control.

Shapes
  Twenty-two starting forms, including superforms, rosettes, organic curves,
  spirals and waves. Edit branches, inset, tension, twist and irregularity.
  There is no fixed limit of 48 parts. Each generated form remains editable.
  Drag to move; corner handles resize; the top handle rotates.
  Shift preserves proportions or snaps rotation to 15-degree steps.
  Arrow keys move the selected part; Shift increases the step; Delete removes.

3D
  Switch between 2D and 3D for lettering, symbols or compositions.
  Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom. Adjust extrusion, bevel, rotation, material,
  side color, outline, lighting, shadows and background in the render panel.
  Boolean contour operations preserve vector cutouts in the actual mesh.
  Geometry is generated in a worker. Rendering sleeps while the scene is
  still and stops when the tab is hidden. The 3D module loads on demand.

Exports
  Standalone SVG paths and masks without fonts. Transparent 2D PNG at 2x.
  The 3D PNG captures the current camera, material and lighting.
  Ctrl/Cmd+Z undoes; Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z or Ctrl/Cmd+Y redoes.
  Designs, render settings and custom colors stay in local browser storage.

Stack
  React 19, React Compiler, TypeScript, Vite, Bun, Jotai, shadcn/Base UI,
  Tailwind CSS, Motion, i18next and Three.js. Fonts are served locally.

Cloudflare
  Pages Direct Upload project: glyphka-plinka.
  Checks run on main pushes and pull requests. Publishing requires a push
  to main by ExtraBinoss with [PUBLISH] in the latest commit message.
  All checks must pass. The deployment uses the verified build artifact.
  Pull requests and manual check runs do not deploy.

  Required repository Actions secrets:
    CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
    CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID

  Configuration: wrangler.jsonc and .github/workflows/ci.yml.
  No credentials are stored in this repository.

Inspiration
  Paul Nicholson's constructions and lettering for Aphex Twin.
  The associated lettering is known as Xylem. Glyphka uses its own generated
  alphabet and parametric geometry.

  https://www.monotype.com/resources/special-aphex-twin-logo
  https://www.factmag.com/2017/02/21/aphex-twin-logo-designer-paul-nicholson-shares-blueprints-iconic-design/

